laude-dev"}}}], "created_at": "2026-10-01T13:51:06Z", "updated_at": "2026-10-01T14:04:36Z", "actor": {"login": "mkondratek", "id": 19799111, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE5Nzk5MTEx", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19799111?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/mkondratek", "html_url": "https://github.com/mkondratek", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/mkondratek/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/mkondratek/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/mkondratek/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/mkondratek/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/mkondratek/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/mkondratek/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/mkondratek/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/mkondratek/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/mkondratek/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "run_attempt": 1, "referenced_workflows": [], "run_started_at": "2026-10-01T13:51:06Z", "triggering_actor": {"login": "mkondratek", "id": 19799111, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE5Nzk5MTEx", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19799111?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/mkondratek", "html_url": "https://github.com/mkondratek", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/mkondratek/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/mkondratek/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/mkondratek/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/mkondratek/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/mkondratek/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/mkondratek/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/mkondratek/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/mkondratek/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/mkondratek/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "jobs_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cline/cline/actions/runs/36871774476/jobs", "logs_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cline/cline/actions/runs/36871774476/logs", "check_suite_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cline/cline/check-suites/99868030796", "artifacts_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cline/cline/actions/runs/36871774476/artifacts", "cancel_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cline/cline/actions/runs/36871774476/cancel", "rerun_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cline/cline/actions/runs/36871774476/rerun", "previous_attempt_url": null, "workflow_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/cline/cline/actions/workflows/275011468", "head_commit": {"id": "ce74ef09141b0e6f3899d6e137659be3308e99b1", "tree_id": "ea6d650ce8969dd72c4b9221e61abaab91d1d090", "message": "fix(vscode): send Cline surface headers from commit message generation (#13593)\n\n* fix(vscode): send Cline surface headers from commit message generation\n\nCommit message generation builds a standalone ApiHandler through\n`buildApiHandler` instead of going through ClineCore, and that path wired\nno request headers at all. The Cline gateway only serves models that are\nrestricted to Cline product surfaces (the free models) to requests that\nidentify themselves, so \"Generate Commit Message with Cline\" failed with\nHTTP 403 on a free model while normal chat on the same model worked.\n\nResolve the headers through the shared `resolveProviderRequestHeaders`\npolicy \u2014 the same one `local-runtime-bootstrap` uses for sessions \u2014 so\nthere stays one source of truth for provider header policy, and attach\nthem to the provider config the standalone handler is built from. The\ncaller now resolves the host client identity first, so a request reports\nthe same client/platform as a task from the same host. Custom provider\nheaders stored in providers.json are layered in as well; the commit path\ndropped those too.\n\nA standalone request is not a task, so no session id is claimed:\n`sessionId` becomes optional in the resolver and `X-Task-ID` is omitted\nrather than sent empty. The pre-SDK extension sent `X-Task-ID: \"\"` from\nthis same code path, so nothing depends on a meaningful id here.\n\nFixes #13590\n\n* refactor(vscode): share one client-identity mapping between sessions and standalone requests\n\n`resolveClineRequestClientContext` mapped the host identity to the SDK's\nclient shape, including the extension-identity fallbacks, and\n`buildSessionConfig` built the same object inline. A commit-message request\nand a task are supposed to report the same client, and two copies of that\nmapping stop guaranteeing it the first time one is edited.\n\nMove the resolver into the session factory and have `buildSessionConfig`\ncall it, so both paths share it by construction. The host-identity and\nmulti-root helpers go back to private.\n\n* fix(vscode): send the core's own version and session source from standalone requests\n\nThe standalone path sent the extension's version as `X-CORE-VERSION` and an\ninlined \"vscode\" source tag, while a task from the same extension sends the\ncore package's version via `local-runtime-bootstrap`. That made the \"same\nheaders as a session\" guarantee untrue for that header, and the reason given\nfor inlining the tag (avoiding a core import) didn't hold: this module already\nsits behind `cline-session-factory`, which imports `@cline/core`.\n\nImport `CORE_BUILD_VERSION` and `SessionSource.VSCODE` from `@cline/core` so\nboth paths agree by construction. The vitest `@cline/core` stub re-exports the\nreal values from SDK source.\n\n* fix(vscode): honor a commit-generation cancel issued while the host identity resolves\n\n`performCommitMsgGeneration` flips the SCM button to its stop action and\nthen awaits `buildApiHandlerWithHostContext()` (two host-bridge lookups)\nbefore it created this generation's `AbortController`. A cancel in that\nwindow aborted the previous controller, if any, and the request the user had\njust cancelled was then sent anyway.\n\nCreate and install the controller before the first await, check it again\nright before `createMessage`, and read it through a local so a later\ngeneration can't swap the signal an earlier one checks. Two small follow-ons\nfrom the same fix: a cancelled generation no longer reports \"Failed to\ngenerate commit message: This operation was aborted\", and only the current\ngeneration clears the context key, so one that settles late can't flip the\nbutton back while a newer one runs.\n\n* fix(vscode): cancel a running commit generation when a new one starts\n\nEach generation now checks its own controller, but the stop action can only\nreach the one stored in the module slot. The Generate keybinding, unlike\nthe SCM button and palette entry, stays live while a generation runs, so a\nsecond invocation replaced the slot and left the first generation\nunstoppable: Stop cancelled the newer request while the older one kept\nwriting into the commit input. Before the per-generation controller both\nread the shared slot, which is why this only surfaced now.\n\nA new generation now aborts the previous one before taking the slot, so at\nmost one runs and Stop reaches it by construction. The aborted one exits\nwithout an error and leaves the context key to the new generation.\n\n* fix(vscode): let Stop cancel every running commit generation instead of the newest\n\nHaving a new generation abort the previous one made Stop reach everything,\nbut it added a rule `main` never had, and it collided with \"Generate for all\nrepositories\": a generation started mid-run aborted the bulk run's current\nrepository, the bulk loop then moved to the next repository, and that one\naborted the newer request. The latest request was lost and a repository was\nskipped.\n\nTrack every running generation in a set instead. Each registers its\ncontroller before its first await and removes it when it settles; Stop\naborts all of them, and the context key stays set while any runs. Nothing\nbut Stop cancels a generation, so concurrent generations (the Generate\nkeybinding stays live while one runs, the bulk loop starts one per\nrepository) no longer cancel each other, and Stop still reaches all of them.\n\n* test(llms): assert Cline surface headers on streaming requests too\n\nThe wire-level test only drove `doGenerate`, but commit-message generation\ncalls `createMessage`, which streams. A regression that dropped the surface\nheaders from streaming requests alone would have kept the test green while\nthe free-model 403 came back. Run the same assertions through `doStream`\n(and check the request really is a streaming one) for both `cline` and\n`cline-pass`.", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T13:51:02Z", "author": {"name": "Miko\u0142aj Kondratek", "email": "19799111+mkondratek@users.noreply.github.com"}, "committer": {"name": "GitHub", "email": "noreply@github.com"}}, "repository": {"id": 824874689, "node_id": "R_kgDOMSqWwQ", "name": "cline", "full_name": "cline/cline", "private": false, "owner": {"login": "cline", "id": 184127137, "node_id": "O_kgDOCvmOoQ", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184127137?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/cline", "html_url": "https://github.com/cline", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cline/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cline/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cline/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cline/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cline/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cline/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cline/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cline/even